From: Javier Catania <jaca101@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:44:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Edit mode: clicking an image frame from text editing
 returns to normal mode

When a text frame was being edited and the user clicked on an image frame,
CanvasMode_Edit::mousePressEvent kept modeEdit for the newly selected image
frame. A subsequent drag then went through CanvasMode_Edit::mouseMoveEvent,
which calls moveImageInFrame(), shifting the image offset inside the frame
instead of moving the frame itself.

Only keep content editing when the newly selected item is a text frame.
Image frames now follow the same path as other items: switch to modeNormal
and forward the press, so the drag moves the frame. Image content editing
remains available via double click.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 scribus/canvasmode_edit.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scribus/canvasmode_edit.cpp b/scribus/canvasmode_edit.cpp
index 994b28c74..188ff4171 100644
--- a/scribus/canvasmode_edit.cpp
+++ b/scribus/canvasmode_edit.cpp
@@ -614,7 +614,10 @@ void CanvasMode_Edit::mousePressEvent(QMouseEvent *m)
 				if (SeleItem(m))
 				{
 					currItem = m_doc->m_Selection->itemAt(0);
-					if ((currItem->isTextFrame()) || (currItem->isImageFrame()))
+					// Only text frames keep content editing when clicked from another frame.
+					// Image frames go back to normal mode so a drag moves the frame rather than
+					// the image offset; image content editing is still entered by double click.
+					if (currItem->isTextFrame())
 					{
 						m_view->requestMode(modeEdit);
 						wantNormal = false;
